{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":483908,"name":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","username":"Jarri81","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/dec6dc/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T09:28:25.328Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-483908-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-483908-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-483908-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-483908-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows PC registered as JPA-GranVía.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince Grok Bot 0.43, local execution is broken in a new way:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eComputer list shows connected\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLocal execution set to Always allow / Permitir siempre\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAny command from the agent fails with “temporarily unreachable” (sometimes then “disconnected”)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRenaming the display label (accented í ↔ plain i) made no difference\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore 0.43 it was also flaky, but different: it would connect for a fraction of a second, then drop. So it never fully worked for me, but 0.43 changed the failure mode from “brief connect then drop” to “listed as connected but never actually reachable.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-483908-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-483908-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot on Windows with a registered local computer (JPA-GranVía)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Local execution to Always allow\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAsk an agent to run a simple command on that PC (e.g. hostname)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve: machine may show as connected in Computers, but the command fails with “temporarily unreachable”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-483908-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-483908-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen the PC is registered and Local execution is Always allow, the agent should be able to run commands on it reliably.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-483908-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-483908-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-483908-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-483908-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.43\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-483908-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-483908-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal PC label: JPA-GranVía (Windows). List shows connected; live command fails with temporarily unreachable / disconnected. Always allow is on. Accent in the name was ruled out.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-483908-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-483908-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T09:56:22.815Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":41.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":170683,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable","display_username":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135897,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable/170683/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":483917,"name":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","username":"Jarri81","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/dec6dc/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T09:40:58.493Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eUpdate: Task Manager shows a normal Electron tree (9× Grok Bot.exe) with exactly one local-exec-daemon (PID 13096, path …\\local-exec-daemon\\main.cjs). ListMachines still shows connected; agent Shell still fails with “temporarily unreachable.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDaemon log keeps looping:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esand-local-exec-daemon started → desktop ownership lost, shutting down\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003euser-computer-provider: ConnectError / DeadlineExceededError\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eoccasional {“error”:“cli_unknown_command”}\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo local helper is up, but the channel isn’t usable. Happy to provide more log lines / Request ID if useful.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T09:40:58.493Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":1.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170683,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable","display_username":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135897,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable/170683/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":483928,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T09:56:12.778Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report and for moving this into a separate thread like Colin asked.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour PC is actually connected, and every command reaches it. What we see on our side is that the response from your PC comes back about 11 seconds after the request, and the agent stops waiting at 10 seconds. That’s why the command gets marked as temporarily unreachable even though it did run. That also explains the “shows connected, but nothing works” situation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is something we’re already tracking, and I’ve shared your case with the team. The wording change in 0.43 from “disconnected” to “temporarily unreachable” is from a separate improvement, not a sign that things got worse.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo help us figure out what’s delaying the response on your side, could you share a few things if you can:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn File Explorer, paste \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\u003c/code\u003e into the address bar, find \u003ccode\u003elocal-exec-daemon.log\u003c/code\u003e, and attach it here (or the last about 200 lines). Please quickly skim it for anything personal before sending.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhat antivirus or endpoint security are you using, just Windows Defender or a third-party product?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIs your Documents or AppData folder redirected to OneDrive or a network drive?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAre you using a VPN or a corporate proxy while using Grok Bot?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo need to rename your computer or toggle Local execution again, it’s not related. I’ll reply in the thread when I have an update.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T09:56:12.778Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":1.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170683,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable/170683/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":484059,"name":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","username":"Jarri81","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/dec6dc/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T13:39:48.104Z","cooked":"\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAntivirus:\u003c/strong\u003e Windows Defender + \u003cstrong\u003eSurfshark Antivirus\u003c/strong\u003e (real-time protection and web protection were on; exclusion list was empty).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVPN / proxy:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eSurfshark VPN\u003c/strong\u003e. No corporate proxy.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOneDrive / redirects:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eDocuments\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003eDesktop\u003c/strong\u003e are redirected to OneDrive . \u003cstrong\u003eAppData\u003c/strong\u003e is local , not redirected.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTest result:\u003c/strong\u003e After disconnecting Surfshark VPN and turning off Surfshark Antivirus real-time + web protection, local commands started succeeding in about \u003cstrong\u003e1.4 seconds\u003c/strong\u003e (agent could run \u003ccode\u003ehostname\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003ewhoami\u003c/code\u003e successfully). So the ~11s delay looks tied to Surfshark.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T13:39:48.104Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":6.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":170683,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable","display_username":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135897,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable/170683/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":484087,"name":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","username":"Jarri81","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/dec6dc/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T14:26:06.606Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eFollow-up.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRoot cause (confirmed):\u003c/strong\u003e Surfshark Antivirus \u003cstrong\u003ereal-time protection\u003c/strong\u003e. Not the VPN, not web protection, not the accented PC name.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eSetup\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eResult\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eSurfshark VPN on, AV real-time off\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eOK (~1.3s)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eWeb protection on, real-time off\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eOK (~3s)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eReal-time on\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003etemporarily unreachable\u003c/code\u003e (matches your ~11s vs 10s timeout)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eReal-time on + exclude only \u003ccode\u003eC:\\Users\\user\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eOK (~1–2s)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhy Temp:\u003c/strong\u003e each local-exec command writes a fresh \u003ccode\u003eps-script-\u0026lt;uuid\u0026gt;.ps1\u003c/code\u003e under \u003ccode\u003e%TEMP%\u003c/code\u003e and runs it via PowerShell. Surfshark real-time inspects that create/execute path and adds enough latency to miss the 10s agent wait. Excluding the Grok Bot install folder alone did \u003cstrong\u003enot\u003c/strong\u003e help. Surfshark also does \u003cstrong\u003enot\u003c/strong\u003e accept wildcard exclusions (e.g. \u003ccode\u003eps-script-*.ps1\u003c/code\u003e), so we can’t narrow to just those scripts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWorkaround we have now:\u003c/strong\u003e exclude all of \u003ccode\u003e%TEMP%\u003c/code\u003e. That works, but it’s a \u003cstrong\u003esecurity trade-off\u003c/strong\u003e — we don’t want real-time AV to ignore everything created in Temp long-term.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat would actually fix this properly (product side):\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBest:\u003c/strong\u003e write local-exec scripts to a dedicated folder (e.g. under \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\\tmp\u003c/code\u003e) so users can exclude only that path while keeping Temp scanned; or\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRaise the local-exec wait timeout above ~11s so a normal AV scan doesn’t trip \u003ccode\u003etemporarily unreachable\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T14:26:06.606Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":0.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":170683,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable","display_username":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135897,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable/170683/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":484139,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T16:38:11.657Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eGreat job debugging this, you basically found the root cause yourself. This is exactly the kind of delay we were looking for. Surfshark (VPN and or real time antivirus) is intercepting and scanning the local daemon channel, so the response from your PC comes back in about 11 seconds instead of a fraction of a second, and the agent stops waiting at 10 seconds. After you disabled it, the delay went away, so the story checks out.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo avoid keeping VPN and antivirus turned off all the time, try a more targeted setup and see if the delay comes back:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Surfshark Antivirus, add the folder \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\u003c/code\u003e to exclusions (especially the process \u003ccode\u003elocal-exec-daemon\\main.cjs\u003c/code\u003e) and also add the Grok Bot executable. Then turn real time protection and web protection back on.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf it still only fails when the VPN is on, it is probably Surfshark VPN routing. Check split tunneling and add Grok Bot to the VPN exclusions so its traffic goes directly.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat should help you figure out which one is causing the delay (AV scanning or VPN routing) and keep protection enabled.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a really useful signal for this issue. Let me know if the exclusions helped, and I will update the thread if there is anything else.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":11,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T16:38:11.657Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":8,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170683,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":135897,"username":"Jarri81","name":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/dec6dc/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable/170683/11","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":484216,"name":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","username":"Jarri81","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/dec6dc/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:48:28.691Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks Dean — quick clarification so we don’t chase the VPN path.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe already A/B’d this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSurfshark VPN on + AV real-time off\u003c/strong\u003e → OK (~1.3s)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWeb protection on + real-time off\u003c/strong\u003e → OK (~3s)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReal-time on\u003c/strong\u003e → \u003ccode\u003etemporarily unreachable\u003c/code\u003e again\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eExcluding \u003cstrong\u003eonly\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003e%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Temp\u003c/code\u003e (with real-time still on) → OK (~1–2s)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eExcluding Grok Bot install / \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\u003c/code\u003e / exe alone was \u003cstrong\u003enot\u003c/strong\u003e enough earlier\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo the delay is \u003cstrong\u003eSurfshark Antivirus real-time\u003c/strong\u003e on the temp \u003ccode\u003eps-script-*.ps1\u003c/code\u003e create/execute path, not VPN routing. Surfshark also doesn’t accept wildcard excludes (can’t do just \u003ccode\u003eps-script-*.ps1\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrent workaround: exclude all of Temp. It works, but it’s a broad security trade-off. Still hoping for a dedicated Grok Bot tmp folder (or a timeout \u0026gt; ~11s) so we can keep Temp scanned.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":12,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-09-05T19:48:28.691Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170683,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable","display_username":"Javier Pérez de Arrilucea","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135897,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-43-windows-local-pc-shows-connected-but-commands-fail-with-temporarily-unreachable/170683/12","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[483908,483917,483928,484059,484087,484139,484216]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1],[4,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"},{"id":407,"name":"remote-control","slug":"remote-control"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot 0.43 Windows — local PC shows connected but commands fail with “temporarily unreachable”","id":170683,"title":"Grok Bot 0.43 Windows — local PC shows connected but commands fail with “temporarily unreachable”","posts_count":7,"created_at":"2026-09-05T09:28:25.269Z